rradius installed from a package
================================

The package installs the program, the RADIUS dictionaries and the documentation, and creates
the system user "rradius" and the directories /var/lib/rradius (data) and /var/log/rradius.
It does not create a configuration and does not start the service: the service starts only
once /etc/rradius/rradius.toml exists.

First start
-----------

  1. Print a starting configuration; it has random cluster and client secrets:

       rradius-server config init > /etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  2. Point "dictionary" at /usr/share/rradius/dictionary, add the [lua] script and your
     clients, and keep the file readable by the "rradius" user only:

       chown root:rradius /etc/rradius/rradius.toml && chmod 640 /etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  3. Check, then start:

       rradius-server check
       systemctl enable --now rradius

The default configuration path is fixed when the program is built; "rradius-server --version"
shows it on the second line.

Documentation: /usr/share/doc/rradius/manual/README.md (start there) and usage.md.
The examples of the manual are in /usr/share/doc/rradius/examples.
